course: dictionary
lesson: 11398
title: Accompanied and what goes with what
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Accompanied is the past form of accompany. It can mean that someone went with you, or that one thing happened together with another.
explain: «The little girl walked to the shop, accompanied by her big brother.» The clues are the little girl and the big brother walking together, so accompanied means went with.
explain: «Thunder accompanied the lightning all night.» Thunder happened at the same time as lightning, so accompanied means came along with it. Ask: what word would fit here? Try went with or happened together with in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «The singer was accompanied by a piano.» The piano played music to support the singer. In music, accompanied means played along to support a singer or another player.
fact: Accompany is the verb, and accompanied is its past form.
fact: «Accompanied» can mean went somewhere with someone.
fact: «Accompanied» can also mean happened or existed together with something else, like «thunder accompanied by lightning».
fact: In music, «accompanied» means played to support a singer or another player.
fact: «Unaccompanied» means without anyone or anything with it, as in «unaccompanied children».
exercise: «The puppy was accompanied by its mother on the walk.» What does accompanied mean here? | Was fed at | Ran away from | *Went with | Was lost by
exercise: «Each child must be accompanied by an adult.» What does this rule mean? | Children must run ahead | Adults must wait outside | Children must be quiet | *Children must go with a grown-up
exercise: «The choir sang, accompanied by a guitar.» What does accompanied mean here? | *Played music to support | Ran behind | Argued with | Stopped
test: «Strong winds accompanied the heavy rain.» What does accompanied mean here? | Happened before | *Happened together with | Stopped | Hid from
test: Ella asks, «What does unaccompanied mean?» What is the answer? | With a big group | Very loud | Lost in a crowd | *Without anyone with you
exam: Maths: «Each child was accompanied by one parent, and there were 12 children. How many people were there in total?» | *24 | 18 | 6 | 12
